== Stage 1 ==
;23 August 2025 – [[Turin]] ([[Palace of Venaria|Reggia di Venaria]]) (Italy) to [[Novara]] (Italy), {{convert|186.1|km|abbr=on}}

The race began with a {{convert|186.1|km|adj=on}} flat stage that was expected to offer an opportunity for the sprinters to take the first red leader’s jersey. There was a lone third-category climb that topped after {{convert|69.8|km|abbr=}} of racing.

As soon as the flag dropped, six riders got a gap on the peloton. The break was composed of [[Koen Bouwman]] ({{UCI team code|JAY men|2025}}), [[Alessandro Verre]] ({{UCI team code|ARK men|2025}}), [[Nicolas Vinokurov]] ({{UCI team code|XAT|2025}}), [[Pepijn Reinderink]] ({{UCI team code|SOQ|2025}}), [[Hugo de la Calle]] ({{UCI team code|BBH|2025}}), and [[Joel Nicolau]] ({{UCI team code|CJR|2025}}). Their advantage over the peloton maxed out at just over two minutes as {{UCI team code|ADC|2025}} and {{UCI team code|LTK men|2025}} took control for their sprinters, [[Jasper Philipsen]] and [[Mads Pedersen (cyclist)|Mads Pedersen]], respectively. At the top of the only categorized climb on the stage, Verre took maximum {{abbr|KOM|King of the Mountains}} points ahead of Nicolau and Vinokourov to take the first polka-dot jersey of the race. At the intermediate sprint with {{convert|90.6|km|abbr=}} left, the break swept up the points and the bonus seconds available. With {{convert|84|km|abbr=}} to go, de la Calle went solo off the front. The five remnants of the break were soon caught by the peloton. As the riders approached the finale of the stage, de la Calle was caught by the peloton at {{convert|37|km|abbr=}} from the finish. The race headed to the inevitable bunch sprint with the sprinters’ teams setting stations at the front of the peloton. In the final sprint, Philipsen launched inside the final {{convert|200|m|abbr=}}, sprinting to the victory ahead of [[Ethan Vernon]] ({{UCI team code|IPT|2025}}) and [[Orluis Aular]] ({{UCI team code|MOV men|2025}}) to take the first red jersey. Pedersen, the other stage favorite, was unable to contest the finish and only took fourteenth on the stage.<ref name="CN-1" /><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cyclingweekly.com/racing/jasper-philipsen-takes-vuelta-a-espana-red-jersey-after-sprinting-to-stage-one-win|title=Jasper Philipsen takes Vuelta a España red jersey after sprinting to stage one win|first=Dan|last=Challis|work=Cycling Weekly|date=23 August 2025|access-date=23 August 2025}}</ref>
